Here is the root cause:
The bug was caused by the `get` method in `Jets3tFileSystemStore.java` not handling the scenario where a requested key does not exist in S3 properly. Instead of returning a null value, it threw an `IOException`, which caused S3 filesystem operations to fail when attempting to retrieve missing blocks.

